Spec: SpecDD Symbol Reference Extractor

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Extract explicit `@` symbol reference candidates from SpecDD text.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDSymbolReferenceExtractor.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDSymbolReferenceExtractor.kt

Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/*
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/SpecDDSymbolReferenceExtractorBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Use `@SpecDDLineClassifier` to avoid comments, blank lines, and section headers.
  Extract symbols only when they start with `@`.
  Expose candidate text without the leading `@`.
  Expose the full source range including the leading `@`.
  Require the first symbol character after `@` to be an ASCII letter or `_`.
  Allow subsequent symbol characters to be ASCII letters, digits, `_`, `.`, `:`, `#`, `\`, `/`, `?`, or `!`.
  Recognize symbols at line start, after whitespace, or after opening punctuation.
  Recognize opening punctuation before `@` as `(`, `[`, `{`, `<`, `"`, or `'`.
  Recognize `@` immediately after an inline code span opening backtick as a code-span symbol reference.
  Ignore escaped `\@` sequences.
  Ignore embedded `@` characters inside larger tokens such as email addresses.
  Trim final sentence `.` or `:` punctuation from the symbol text and source range when the next source character is whitespace, end of line, or closing punctuation.
  Recognize symbol references in body entries, task text, scenario steps, key-value lines, continuation lines, and inline code spans.
  Validate line-by-line for LF, CR, and CRLF line endings.
  Cover plain symbols, dotted symbols, symbols with formal punctuation, escaped at signs, embedded at signs, comments, section headers, final sentence punctuation, opening punctuation, and inline code spans in tests.

Must not:
  Resolve symbols.
  Report diagnostics.
  Extract symbols without an explicit `@`.
